\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The counterexample: with $V_1 = \mathrm  {CZ}(A_0,A_1)$, migrating $A_1$ turns the layer into $\mathrm  {CZ}(A_0, e)$ --- the gate drawn here between the top wire (chip A) and the bottom wire (chip B) crosses the cut, so the 2-traversal scheme fails.}}{4}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
